From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: add TX inter-packet pacing and increase buffer retry

C6 SDIO slave SLC DMA descriptor reload takes ~1ms after a Wi-Fi transmission.
Rapid packet bursts (such as Dropbear SSH post-exec sequence with TCP_NODELAY)
exhaust slave buffers and trigger unrecoverable SLC desync if sent back-to-back.
Increase MAX_WRITE_RETRIES from 2 to 50 with 100-200us delay, retry on token read
error, and pace transmissions with 1-2ms delay after each packet.
---
 sdio/esp_sdio.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #include "esp_kernel_port.h"
 
 extern u32 raw_tp_mode;
-#define MAX_WRITE_RETRIES       2
+#define MAX_WRITE_RETRIES       50
 #define TX_MAX_PENDING_COUNT    200
 #define TX_RESUME_THRESHOLD     (TX_MAX_PENDING_COUNT/5)
 
@@ -1018,11 +1018,11 @@
 		while (retry) {
 			ret = esp_slave_get_tx_buffer_num(context, &buf_available, ACQUIRE_LOCK);
 
-			if (buf_available < buf_needed) {
+			if (ret || buf_available < buf_needed) {
 
 				/* Release SDIO and retry after delay*/
 				retry--;
-				usleep_range(10, 50);
+				usleep_range(100, 200);
 				continue;
 			}
 
@@ -1181,6 +1181,9 @@
 
 		dev_kfree_skb(tx_skb);
 		tx_skb = NULL;
+
+		/* Inter-packet pacing: ensure C6 SLC DMA has breathing room between packets */
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
 	}
 
 	do_exit(0);
